.","setup":"The stock rose about 50% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 12 weeks, peaking at $15.12 and pulling back 37% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jul 27, 2006 it closed at $15.23, its first close above the base high of $15.12. Volume that day was 1.9M shares, 0.62x the prior 10-day average of 3.1M. It never committed. The best close afterward was $15.69, within 5% of the level, and the chart ends at $15.51.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakout that never resolved. Price chopped around the level without committing either way. Sitting it out, or getting out flat, was a fine read."}}